title: A Front Gives Way
subtitle: One of the Republic's fronts has broken, one way or the other.
tags: event
view-if: war and front_ev_ready and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 3
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_war.svg
on-arrival: {! SW.frontEvent(Q); !}

= [+ fe_heading +]

[? if fe_lib and fe_front = "outer" : The sieges of the Outer Rim are broken. Republic forces relieve world after world, and some of the systems that seceded raise the Republic's flag again. The Rim remembers who came for it. ?][? if not fe_lib and fe_front = "outer" : The Outer Rim front collapses. Besieged worlds surrender to the Confederacy one by one, refugees choke the hyperlanes, and the Rimward wing asks why the Republic let it happen. ?][? if fe_lib and fe_front = "mid" : The Hydian Way is clear. Convoys run from the Core to the Rim again, Mid Rim worlds that had drifted to the Confederacy come back, and freight rates fall across the Republic. ?][? if not fe_lib and fe_front = "mid" : The Hydian Way falls to the Confederacy. Mid Rim worlds change sides, freighters stop running, and the Republic's trade begins to choke. ?][? if fe_lib and fe_front = "core" : The Separatist raids on the Core approaches are broken at Anaxes. For the first time in the war, Coruscant sleeps easily. ?][? if not fe_lib and fe_front = "core" : Separatist fleets raid the Core approaches, striking the shipyards at Kuat and Corellia. Coruscant panics, and the Navy is blamed. ?]

*When a front breaks, worlds change sides. The War Council's choices decide which fronts hold.*
